    "findings": [
      "21a-1 opaque single top surface contrasts with three translucent red/blue/red layers on separate projected bases. Their opacity grows during narration; layered rear contributions remain visible. Labels identify a teaching diagram, not physical-medium simulation.",
      "21a-2 front red/back blue/output purple blocks have projected front and side faces; yellow connections advance. C=alpha*Cfront+(1-alpha)*Cback and opacity label remain readable. The purple block illustrates output role rather than an asserted measured RGB result. Absorption and opacity distinction retained.",
      "21a-4 two spatial cross-sections retain red in front at pixelA and blue in front at pixelB; connecting arrow grows. This is per-pixel ordering versus object-center sorting, not an observed engine transparency implementation.",
      "21a-5 stacked teal/blue/red source layers link in front-to-back order to corresponding layer1/2/3 outputs. Output blocks rise and successive yellow arrows advance. Added passes and linked-list storage/sort/memory costs are explicit. Samples show no layer-color/order error or label clipping.",
      "857old/858new,1665old/1666new,2423old/2424new; last3221 remains21a-5. All11boards42samples directly read. Clean black/white/yellow explanation, genuine projected top/front/side faces, no burned narration captions. Continuous motion and final composite remain pending."
